.TH DOUBLE-TAP-SWITCHER 1 "November 2026" "Double Tap Switcher 1.39" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
double-tap-switcher \- switch keyboard layouts with configurable double taps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B double-tap-switcher
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Native Qt frontend and GNOME Shell bridge for Ubuntu GNOME 50.
Configure trigger keys and their target layouts in Settings.
Run the application as the desktop user, not as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start without opening Settings; an existing manually stopped hook stays stopped.
.TP
.B --quit
Request normal termination of the current user's running instance.
.TP
.B --start
Request that the current instance start its hook.
.TP
.B --about
Show application information.
.TP
.B --report-bug
Open the user's mail handler with a draft bug report. Nothing is sent automatically.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Password-field protection depends on desktop metadata and is best effort.
A background hidden-input terminal may pause switching globally.
After installation, log out and back in if GNOME cannot load the tray bridge.
